# PDP gallery: Stickers portrait vs Market S landscape (learned 2026-09-25)

## Symptom

Market S detail gallery looks almost like the uploaded file. Stickers — especially **Mixed Labels** — look heavily zoomed; full sheet not visible.

## Not the cause

- Separate Stickers vs HotGoods gallery components (both use `ProductGallery` → `ProductImageZoomPan`)
- Wrong thumbnail URL as main slide (main uses `webpUrl` → `url`; thumbs may `object-cover`)
- Mixed-labels-only PDP route (customize is separate; PDP is still `/products/[id]`)

## Real cause

| | Mixed Labels (example) | Market S (typical) |
|--|------------------------|--------------------|
| Aspect | Portrait (e.g. 769×1095, some 3703×5529) | Landscape pack shot |
| Same CSS `w-full` + box `maxHeight` + `overflow-hidden` | Fills width, **clips** top/bottom | Fills width, full art still in view |

So Market S “looks correct” and Stickers “look zoomed” on **identical** gallery code — asset shape differs.

## Invariant

Main PDP slide must show **full artwork** with `object-contain`, sizing by **`max-height` + `width: auto`** (not `width: 100%` inside a height-clipped overflow box). Clip with `overflow-hidden` **only while click-zoom is active**.

## Do not

- Switch main slide to `object-cover` to “match Market S fullness”
- Re-add container `minHeight: 400` + img `h-full` on the zoom wrapper
- Assume Mixed Labels needs a different gallery component — fix shared zoom-pan sizing instead
